<% content_for :title, "Papi, API specs with a review workflow" %>

<section class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-20">
  <h1 class="display max-w-3xl text-[44px] leading-[1.1] tracking-tight text-slate-900">
    Swagger, but better
  </h1>
  <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
    Papi does the job OpenAPI does: it describes an HTTP API. It adds the things
    OpenAPI never had. A review workflow. A diff that understands schemas. Comments
    that survive the next version. A mock server that answers real requests.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8 flex items-center gap-3">
    <%= link_to "Read the blog", posts_path,
          class: "rounded border border-sky-800 bg-sky-700 px-4 py-2 text-[13px] font-semibold text-white no-underline hover:bg-sky-800" %>
    <%= link_to "Get access", demo_access_path,
          class: "rounded border border-slate-400 px-4 py-2 text-[13px] font-semibold text-slate-700 no-underline hover:bg-slate-50" %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="border-y border-slate-400 bg-slate-50">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-16">
    <h2 class="display text-[28px] tracking-tight">A schema is one line</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
      Objects, arrays, unions, optional attributes and references to named entities,
      in a grammar you can read out loud. The whole schema is one string.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div class="rounded border border-slate-400 bg-white">
        <div class="border-b border-slate-200 px-4 py-2 text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-slate-600">Papi</div>
        <pre class="overflow-x-auto px-4 py-4 font-mono text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-slate-800">{id:number,customer:Customer,tags?:[string]}</pre>
      </div>
      <div class="rounded border border-slate-400 bg-white">
        <div class="border-b border-slate-200 px-4 py-2 text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-slate-600">OpenAPI</div>
<pre class="overflow-x-auto px-4 py-4 font-mono text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-slate-800">type: object
required: [id, customer]
properties:
  id:
    type: number
  customer:
    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Customer'
  tags:
    type: array
    items:
      type: string</pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-16">
  <h2 class="display text-[28px] tracking-tight">A spec change is a pull request</h2>
  <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
    Nothing lands because someone committed it. A change opens as a candidate against
    the current version, gets read, argued over and approved, and only then merges into
    a version of its own.
  </p>

  <ol class="mt-8 grid gap-px border border-slate-400 bg-slate-200 md:grid-cols-4">
    <% [
         [ "Open", "A candidate carries one draft version, edited in place. There is no per-edit history to wade through." ],
         [ "Review", "Threads sit beside the thing they are about. A reordered object never asks to be reviewed." ],
         [ "Approve", "One thumbs up per reader, and never the author's own." ],
         [ "Merge", "An admin promotes the draft, and it becomes the published version everyone reads." ]
       ].each_with_index do |(title, body), index| %>
      <li class="bg-white p-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] tabular-nums text-slate-500"><%= index + 1 %></div>
        <h3 class="display mt-1 text-[17px] tracking-tight"><%= title %></h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600"><%= body %></p>
      </li>
    <% end %>
  </ol>
</section>

<section class="border-t border-slate-400 bg-slate-50">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-6 py-16">
    <h2 class="display text-[28px] tracking-tight">A change, read by the tool</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
      One candidate against the version it came from, laid out the way Papi lays it out.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 rounded border border-slate-400 bg-white">
      <div class="grid border-b border-slate-200 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="border-slate-200 px-4 py-2 text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-slate-600 md:border-r">v3</div>
        <div class="px-4 py-2 text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-slate-600">rc4</div>
      </div>

      <div class="grid gap-4 p-4 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-md bg-slate-50 py-2 ring-1 ring-inset ring-slate-200">
          <div class="flex min-h-[18px] border-l-2 border-transparent pr-2.5">
            <span class="w-8 shrink-0 select-none pr-2 text-right font-mono text-[11px] leading-[18px] text-slate-500">1</span>
            <span class="whitespace-pre font-mono text-[12px] leading-[18px] text-slate-700">{</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex min-h-[18px] border-l-2 border-transparent pr-2.5">
            <span class="w-8 shrink-0 select-none pr-2 text-right font-mono text-[11px] leading-[18px] text-slate-500">2</span>
            <span class="whitespace-pre font-mono text-[12px] leading-[18px] text-slate-700">  id: <span class="rounded px-1 ring-1 ring-inset bg-blue-100 text-blue-800 ring-blue-200">number</span></span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex min-h-[18px] border-l-2 border-transparent pr-2.5">
            <span class="w-8 shrink-0 select-none pr-2 text-right font-mono text-[11px] leading-[18px] text-slate-500">3</span>
            <span class="whitespace-pre font-mono text-[12px] leading-[18px] text-slate-700">  email: <span class="rounded px-1 ring-1 ring-inset bg-green-100 text-green-800 ring-green-200">string</span></span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex min-h-[18px] border-l-2 border-amber-500 bg-amber-100 pr-2.5">
            <span class="w-8 shrink-0 select-none pr-2 text-right font-mono text-[11px] leading-[18px] text-slate-500">4</span>
            <span class="whitespace-pre font-mono text-[12px] leading-[18px] text-slate-700">  status: <span class="rounded px-1 ring-1 ring-inset bg-green-100 text-green-800 ring-green-200">string</span></span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex min-h-[18px] border-l-2 border-rose-500 bg-rose-100 pr-2.5">
            <span class="w-8 shrink-0 select-none pr-2 text-right font-mono text-[11px] leading-[18px] text-slate-500">5</span>
            <span class="whitespace-pre font-mono text-[12px] leading-[18px] text-slate-700">  legacyRef: <span class="rounded px-1 ring-1 ring-inset bg-green-100 text-green-800 ring-green-200">string</span></span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex min-h-[18px] border-l-2 border-transparent pr-2.5">
            <span class="w-8 shrink-0 select-none pr-2 text-right font-mono text-[11px] leading-[18px] text-slate-500"></span>
            <span class="whitespace-pre font-mono text-[12px] leading-[18px] text-slate-700"> </span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex min-h-[18px] border-l-2 border-transparent pr-2.5">
            <span class="w-8 shrink-0 select-none pr-2 text-right font-mono text-[11px] leading-[18px] text-slate-500">6</span>
            <span class="whitespace-pre font-mono text-[12px] leading-[18px] text-slate-700">}</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-md bg-slate-50 py-2 ring-1 ring-inset ring-slate-200">
          <div class="flex min-h-[18px] border-l-2 border-transparent pr-2.5">
            <span class="w-8 shrink-0 select-none pr-2 text-right font-mono text-[11px] leading-[18px] text-slate-500">1</span>
            <span class="whitespace-pre font-mono text-[12px] leading-[18px] text-slate-700">{</span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex min-h-[18px] border-l-2 border-transparent pr-2.5">
            <span class="w-8 shrink-0 select-none pr-2 text-right font-mono text-[11px] leading-[18px] text-slate-500">2</span>
            <span class="whitespace-pre font-mono text-[12px] leading-[18px] text-slate-700">  id: <span class="rounded px-1 ring-1 ring-inset bg-blue-100 text-blue-800 ring-blue-200">number</span></span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex min-h-[18px] border-l-2 border-transparent pr-2.5">
            <span class="w-8 shrink-0 select-none pr-2 text-right font-mono text-[11px] leading-[18px] text-slate-500">3</span>
            <span class="whitespace-pre font-mono text-[12px] leading-[18px] text-slate-700">  email: <span class="rounded px-1 ring-1 ring-inset bg-green-100 text-green-800 ring-green-200">string</span></span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex min-h-[18px] border-l-2 border-amber-500 bg-amber-100 pr-2.5">
            <span class="w-8 shrink-0 select-none pr-2 text-right font-mono text-[11px] leading-[18px] text-slate-500">4</span>
            <span class="whitespace-pre font-mono text-[12px] leading-[18px] text-slate-700">  status: <span class="rounded px-1 ring-1 ring-inset bg-violet-100 text-violet-800 ring-violet-300">Status</span></span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex min-h-[18px] border-l-2 border-transparent pr-2.5">
            <span class="w-8 shrink-0 select-none pr-2 text-right font-mono text-[11px] leading-[18px] text-slate-500"></span>
            <span class="whitespace-pre font-mono text-[12px] leading-[18px] text-slate-700"> </span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex min-h-[18px] border-l-2 border-emerald-500 bg-emerald-100 pr-2.5">
            <span class="w-8 shrink-0 select-none pr-2 text-right font-mono text-[11px] leading-[18px] text-slate-500">5</span>
            <span class="whitespace-pre font-mono text-[12px] leading-[18px] text-slate-700">  trialEndsAt?: <span class="rounded px-1 ring-1 ring-inset bg-green-100 text-green-800 ring-green-200">string</span></span>
          </div>
          <div class="flex min-h-[18px] border-l-2 border-transparent pr-2.5">
            <span class="w-8 shrink-0 select-none pr-2 text-right font-mono text-[11px] leading-[18px] text-slate-500">6</span>
            <span class="whitespace-pre font-mono text-[12px] leading-[18px] text-slate-700">}</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
      <code class="font-mono text-[13px] text-slate-800">status</code> went from a bare
      string to a named entity, <code class="font-mono text-[13px] text-slate-800">legacyRef</code>
      is gone, and an optional attribute arrived. The blank rows are the diff holding
      both columns in step, so a line and the line it replaced sit level with each
      other.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
      <div>
        <h3 class="display text-[19px] tracking-tight">A thread anchored to a line</h3>
        <div class="mt-4 rounded border border-slate-400 bg-white p-4">
          <div class="mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="truncate text-[13px] font-semibold text-slate-800">anka@example.com</span>
            <span class="shrink-0 rounded-full border border-slate-200 px-1.5 text-[11px] font-medium text-slate-600">Author</span>
            <span class="ml-auto shrink-0 text-[12px] text-slate-600">4 Sep 2026</span>
          </div>
          <div class="whitespace-pre-wrap text-[13px] leading-6 text-slate-700">Making status an entity means every endpoint that returns one moves together. That is the point, but it is a breaking change for anyone parsing the string.</div>

          <div class="mt-3 border-l-2 border-slate-200 pl-3">
            <div class="mb-1 flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="truncate text-[13px] font-semibold text-slate-800">tomek@example.com</span>
              <span class="ml-auto shrink-0 text-[12px] text-slate-600">5 Sep 2026</span>
            </div>
            <div class="whitespace-pre-wrap text-[13px] leading-6 text-slate-700">Agreed. Worth its own version rather than riding along with the trial field.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
          The thread is fixed to <em>that line of that response</em>, by what it is
          rather than by a row id. Cutting a new version copies every record and
          gives it fresh ids; the thread is still on the line it was about.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h3 class="display text-[19px] tracking-tight">The spec answers</h3>
        <div class="mt-4 overflow-hidden rounded border border-slate-400 bg-white">
          <div class="overflow-x-auto bg-slate-900 px-4 py-3 font-mono text-[12px] leading-relaxed text-slate-100">$ curl "…/candidates/rc4/customers/42"</div>
          <div class="overflow-x-auto px-4 py-3 font-mono text-[12px] leading-relaxed text-slate-800">{
  "id": 0,
  "email": "abc",
  "status": { "code": "abc" },
  "trialEndsAt": "abc"
}</div>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-slate-600">
          The declared responses are a running mock server. A published version serves
          under its own URL and so does an open candidate, so this proposal is callable
          while it is still being argued about.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
